    <string name="set_credentials_body">The addresses, usernames and passwords for your NAS, WebDAV or media servers live on this computer only — encrypted with a key in the system keychain — are used to reach your own servers, and are never uploaded.</string>
    <string name="set_no_collect_body">Reality NAS Player has no accounts and carries no analytics, tracking or advertising. Your files, the list of them, what you watched and what you saved live on this computer alone, unless you turn on sync — and then only on your own NAS.</string>
    <string name="set_about_line">Reality NAS Player · a poster wall for your library</string>
    <string name="set_about_body">Reality NAS Player turns the tangle of video files on this computer and your NAS into a poster wall, and plays them — anything mpv can play, which is nearly everything. Free and open source.</string>
